{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11ff1518c1c4989","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Deterministic pre-submit validation for one strategy's epic decomposition.\n3\t\n4\tChecks the mechanically decidable contract rules that the downstream judges\n5\tand submit.py enforce — the ones an LLM step can silently get wrong while the\n6\tdecomposition still looks good:\n7\t\n8\t  1. Epic body sections: every epic file must carry headings covering\n9\t     Description, Scope, Acceptance Criteria, and HLR Traceability (matched on\n10\t     heading text at any level, exactly like the artifact contract).\n11\t  2. Component vocabulary: every epic's `component` frontmatter value must be\n12\t     verbatim in .context/rhai-components.txt (submit.py silently strips\n13\t     unknown names, leaving the Jira epic component-less).\n14\t  3. Rule 11 (docs-last): every docs-authoring epic must be blocked, directly\n15\t     or transitively, by every main-plan Implementation epic that is not\n16\t     itself docs-authoring.\n17\t  4. Priority inheritance: an epic that directly or transitively enables a P0\n18\t     epic must itself be P0 (docs-authoring epics are exempt; branch epics\n19\t     are conditional alternatives and out of scope).\n20\t  5. Implementation-type parallelism (Rules 7/8/10): no `dependencies` edge,\n21\t     in either direction, between a license-validation and a repo-onboarding\n22\t     epic (Rule 7), a license-validation and a konflux-onboarding epic\n23\t     (Rule 8), or a konflux-onboarding and a general implementation epic\n24\t     (Rule 10) — these pairs must run in parallel; any real coupling is an\n25\t     acceptance-criterion gate, never a DAG edge. Edges into a docs-authoring\n26\t     epic are exempt (Rule 11 requires them).\n27\t  6. Epic-size overage triggers (summary-side): a decomposition summary that\n28\t     acknowledges an epic kept above the ~2-week guideline must record a\n29\t     concrete re-split trigger somewhere in the summary — a bare\n30\t     \"flagged for planning awareness only\" note is an unresolved defect.\n31\t  7. On-matrix bundling record (summary-side): when the summary acknowledges a\n32\t     lower-priority HLR bundled into a higher-priority epic, the HLR\n33\t     Traceability Matrix row itself must carry the `bundled` flag with its\n34\t     rationale — a rationale that lives only in prose outside the matrix reads\n35\t     as an unanalyzed priority collapse.\n36\t\n37\tExit 0 with \"OK\" when clean; exit 1 with one line per violation otherwise.\n38\t\n39\tUsage:\n40\t    python3 skills/epic-decompose/scripts/validate_decomposition.py <STRAT_ID> \\\n41\t        [--artifacts-dir artifacts] [--components .context/rhai-components.txt]\n42\t    python3 skills/epic-decompose/scripts/validate_decomposition.py --self-check\n43\t\"\"\"\n44\t\n45\timport argparse\n46\timport os\n47\timport re\n48\timport sys\n49\t\n50\timport yaml\n51\t\n52\tSECTIONS = [(\"Description\", (\"description\",)),\n53\t            (\"Scope\", (\"scope\",)),\n54\t            (\"Acceptance Criteria\", (\"acceptance criteria\",)),\n55\t            (\"HLR Traceability\", (\"hlr traceability\", \"traceability\"))]\n56\t\n57\tPRIORITY_ORDER = {\"P0\": 0, \"P1\": 1, \"P2\": 2}\n58\t\n59\tIT_ENUM = (\"docs-authoring\", \"konflux-onboarding\", \"license-validation\",\n60\t           \"repo-onboarding\")\n61\t\n62\t# Pairs of implementation kinds that must run in parallel (no DAG edge either\n63\t# way) — parity with the implementation_type_rules judge.\n64\tPARALLEL_PAIRS = {\n65\t    frozenset((\"license-validation\", \"repo-onboarding\")): \"Rule 7\",\n66\t    frozenset((\"license-validation\", \"konflux-onboarding\")): \"Rule 8\",\n67\t    frozenset((\"konflux-onboarding\", \"general\")): \"Rule 10\",\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\tFRONTMATTER_RE = re.compile(r'^---\\s*\\n(.*?\\n)---\\s*\\n', re.DOTALL)\n71\t\n72\t# ─── check 6: epic-size overage triggers (summary-side) ───────────────────────\n73\t# A segment \"acknowledges a kept overage\" when it says the work sits above the\n74\t# size guideline. Negations (\"stays within the guideline\") never acknowledge.\n75\tOVERAGE_ACK = re.compile(\n76\t    r'\\b(?:above|exceeds?|exceeded|over|beyond|larger than|'\n77\t    r'at (?:or )?(?:slightly )?above|at the upper (?:end|bound) of)\\s*'\n78\t    r'[^.\\n]{0,80}?\\b(?:guideline|2-week|two-week|one[- ]sprint|'\n79\t    r'epic[- ]size|size guideline)\\b', re.I)\n80\tOVERAGE_NEG = re.compile(\n81\t    r'\\b(?:within|stays? within|does not exceed|no epic (?:exceeds|is above)|'\n82\t    r'under)\\s*[^.\\n]{0,60}?\\b(?:guideline|2-week|size)\\b', re.I)\n83\t# A re-split trigger is a conditional planning statement naming when to split.\n84\tRESPLIT_TRIG = re.compile(\n85\t    r'\\bre-?split\\b|'\n86\t    r'\\bsplit\\b[^.\\n]{0,120}\\bif\\b|'\n87\t    r'\\bif\\b[^.\\n]{0,120}\\b(?:outgrows|exceeds the|finds (?:materially )?more|'\n88\t    r'grows beyond|expands beyond)\\b', re.I)\n89\t\n90\t# ─── check 7: on-matrix bundling record (summary-side) ────────────────────────\n91\t# Fires only when the summary itself acknowledges a bundling DECISION (the\n92\t# word \"bundled\" near an HLR id or a P0/P1/P2 label) in prose outside the\n93\t# matrix, while no matrix row carries the flag.\n94\tBUNDLE_ACK = re.compile(\n95\t    r'\\bbundl\\w*\\b[^.\\n]{0,100}\\b(?:P[012]\\b|HLR|priority)|'\n96\t    r'\\b(?:HLR|P[12]\\b|priority)[^.\\n]{0,100}\\bbundl\\w*\\b', re.I)\n97\t# An off-matrix bundling note that itself carries the why-not-splittable\n98\t# rationale is a compliant record; only a bare pointer is a violation.\n99\t# (\"same component/team\" is deliberately NOT a rationale marker — it restates\n100\t# the default boundary rule, not why the HLR is not separately schedulable.)\n101\tBUNDLE_RATIONALE = re.compile(\n102\t    r'\\b(?:because|since|shares?|shared|extends? the same|thin layer|'\n103\t    r'same (?:call|report|data|surface|file|ui|endpoint|code|site)|'\n104\t    r'not (?:independently|separately) (?:deferrable|schedulable)|'\n105\t    r'double-touch|two (?:epics|passes|audits)|'\n106\t    r'duplicat\\w+ the (?:audit|work|pass)|fragment\\w+)\\b', re.I)\n107\tMATRIX_ROW_BUNDLED = re.compile(r'^\\s*\\|.*\\bbundl', re.I | re.M)\n108\tMATRIX_RE = re.compile(r'#+\\s*HLR Traceability Matrix.*?(?=\\n#|\\Z)', re.S)\n109\t\n110\t\n111\tdef read_frontmatter(path):\n112\t    \"\"\"Return (frontmatter dict, body string) for a markdown file.\"\"\"\n113\t    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n114\t        content = f.read()\n115\t    m = FRONTMATTER_RE.match(content)\n116\t    if not m:\n117\t        return {}, content\n118\t    try:\n119\t        data = yaml.safe_load(m.group(1))\n120\t    except yaml.YAMLError:\n121\t        return {}, content\n122\t    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n123\t        return {}, content\n124\t    return data, content[m.end():]\n125\t\n126\t\n127\tdef body_headings(body):\n128\t    heads = []\n129\t    for hm in re.finditer(r'^#{1,6}\\s+(.+?)\\s*$', body, re.M):\n130\t        heads.append(re.sub(r'[^a-z ]', '', hm.group(1).lower()).strip())\n131\t    return heads\n132\t\n133\t\n134\tdef load_epics(artifacts_dir, strat_id):\n135\t    \"\"\"Return {epic_key: (path, frontmatter, body)} for one strategy's epics.\n136\t\n137\t    epic_key is the filename stem; branch files carry their BRANCH- prefix.\n138\t    \"\"\"\n139\t    task_dir = os.path.join(artifacts_dir, \"epic-tasks\")\n140\t    if not os.path.isdir(task_dir):\n141\t        return {}\n142\t    pat = re.compile(re.escape(strat_id) + r\"-(BRANCH-[A-Z]-)?(E\\d{3})\\.md$\")\n143\t    epics = {}\n144\t    for name in sorted(os.listdir(task_dir)):\n145\t        m = pat.match(name)\n146\t        if not m:\n147\t            continue\n148\t        path = os.path.join(task_dir, name)\n149\t        fm, body = read_frontmatter(path)\n150\t        epics[name[:-3]] = (path, fm, body)\n151\t    return epics\n152\t\n153\t\n154\tdef dependency_closure(start_key, deps):\n155\t    \"\"\"All epics reachable from start_key by following dependencies.\"\"\"\n156\t    seen, stack = set(), list(deps.get(start_key, []))\n157\t    while stack:\n158\t        n = stack.pop()\n159\t        if n in seen or n not in deps:\n160\t            continue\n161\t        seen.add(n)\n162\t        stack.extend(deps[n])\n163\t    return seen\n164\t\n165\t\n166\tdef check(strat_id, artifacts_dir, components_path):\n167\t    \"\"\"Run all checks; return a list of violation strings.\"\"\"\n168\t    probs = []\n169\t    epics = load_epics(artifacts_dir, strat_id)\n170\t    if not epics:\n171\t        return [\"no epic files found for %s under %s/epic-tasks/\"\n172\t                % (strat_id, artifacts_dir)]\n173\t\n174\t    valid_components = set()\n175\t    if os.path.isfile(components_path):\n176\t        with open(components_path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n177\t            valid_components = {ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip()}\n178\t    if not valid_components:\n179\t        probs.append(\"cannot read canonical component list %s — verify the \"\n180\t                     \"path before trusting component names\" % components_path)\n181\t\n182\t    deps, is_branch, is_docs, is_impl, itype, prio = {}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}\n183\t    for key, (path, fm, body) in epics.items():\n184\t        name = key + \".md\"\n185\t        # 1. body sections (contract parity with the artifact judge)\n186\t        heads = body_headings(body)\n187\t        for want, aliases in SECTIONS:\n188\t            if not any(a in h for h in heads for a in aliases):\n189\t                probs.append(\"%s: body missing '%s' section (required \"\n190\t                             \"sections: Description, Scope, Acceptance \"\n191\t                             \"Criteria, HLR Traceability)\" % (name, want))\n192\t        # 2. component vocabulary\n193\t        comp = fm.get(\"component\")\n194\t        if valid_components and isinstance(comp, str) and comp.strip() \\\n195\t                and comp.strip() not in valid_components:\n196\t            probs.append(\"%s: component '%s' is not in %s — pick the closest \"\n197\t                         \"canonical name (submit.py strips unknown names)\"\n198\t                         % (name, comp.strip(), components_path))\n199\t        # collect graph facts\n200\t        dl = fm.get(\"dependencies\")\n201\t        deps[key] = [x for x in dl if isinstance(x, str)] \\\n202\t            if isinstance(dl, list) else []\n203\t        is_branch[key] = \"BRANCH-\" in key\n204\t        is_docs[key] = fm.get(\"implementation_type\") == \"docs-authoring\"\n205\t        is_impl[key] = fm.get(\"type\") == \"Implementation\"\n206\t        it = fm.get(\"implementation_type\")\n207\t        itype[key] = it if it in IT_ENUM else None\n208\t        prio[key] = fm.get(\"priority\")\n209\t\n210\t    def kind(key):\n211\t        \"\"\"Implementation kind of an epic — parity with the judge: an epic\n212\t        that is not type Implementation is never a parallel-rule party; an\n213\t        Implementation epic's kind is its implementation_type when that is a\n214\t        known label, else 'general'.\"\"\"\n215\t        if not is_impl[key]:\n216\t            return \"non-implementation\"\n217\t        return itype[key] or \"general\"\n218\t\n219\t    # 3. Rule 11 — docs-authoring blocked by every main-plan Implementation\n220\t    universe = [k for k in epics\n221\t                if is_impl[k] and not is_docs[k] and not is_branch[k]]\n222\t    for k in sorted(epics):\n223\t        if not is_docs[k]:\n224\t            continue\n225\t        cl = dependency_closure(k, deps)\n226\t        missing = sorted(e for e in universe if e != k and e not in cl)\n227\t        if missing:\n228\t            probs.append(\"Rule 11: docs-authoring %s is not blocked by every \"\n229\t                         \"Implementation epic — add %s to its dependency chain\"\n230\t                         % (k, \", \".join(missing)))\n231\t\n232\t    # 4. Priority inheritance — enablers of P0 work must be P0\n233\t    for k in sorted(epics):\n234\t        if is_branch[k] or is_docs[k]:\n235\t            continue\n236\t        if prio.get(k) != \"P0\":\n237\t            continue\n238\t        # every main-plan, non-docs epic in k's closure enables P0 work\n239\t        cl = dependency_closure(k, deps)\n240\t        for t in sorted(cl):\n241\t            if is_branch[t] or is_docs[t]:\n242\t                continue\n243\t            if PRIORITY_ORDER.get(prio.get(t), 9) > 0:\n244\t                probs.append(\"priority inheritance: %s (%s) blocks P0 epic %s \"\n245\t                             \"but is %s — raise it to P0 or restructure\"\n246\t                             % (t, prio.get(t), k, prio.get(t)))\n247\t\n248\t    # 5. Rules 7/8/10 — implementation-type parallelism: the mandated-parallel\n249\t    #    pairs carry no dependencies edge in either direction (direct edges\n250\t    #    only; edges into a docs-authoring epic are exempt — Rule 11 requires\n251\t    #    them; dependencies naming epics with no file cannot be judged).\n252\t    for k in sorted(epics):\n253\t        if kind(k) == \"docs-authoring\":\n254\t            continue\n255\t        for t in deps[k]:\n256\t            if t not in epics:\n257\t                continue\n258\t            pair = frozenset((kind(t), kind(k)))\n259\t            rule = PARALLEL_PAIRS.get(pair)\n260\t            if rule:\n261\t                probs.append(\"%s: %s (%s) blocks %s (%s) — these must run in \"\n262\t                             \"parallel; remove the dependencies edge and \"\n263\t                             \"express any coupling as an AC gate on the \"\n264\t                             \"dependent epic\"\n265\t                             % (rule, t, kind(t), k, kind(k)))\n266\t\n267\t    # 6. Epic-size overage triggers — a summary that acknowledges an epic kept\n268\t    #    above the ~