y (HLR-1) and both P0 tutorial epics (HLR-2), so it cannot be planned at P1. |\n60\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers using the gallery and the contribution process for new tutorials | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 — scheduled at P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1); docs epics do not push priority upstream. |\n61\t\n62\t## Health Warnings\n63\t\n64\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no per-component\n65\t  change/owner detail in Affected Components (a bare list), no Dependencies table, no\n66\t  Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements. Owner teams\n67\t  were inferred from the architecture-context owning-team fields (Dashboard → RHOAI\n68\t  Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines).\n69\t  Per-epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs.\n70\t- **Priority elevation of HLR-3 (P1 → P0 epic)**: recorded in the matrix row above — the\n71\t  packaging format gates all P0 work, so priority inheritance raises it. This is\n72\t  rule-mandated, not an inversion.\n73\t- **Planning note (epic size)**: the notebook tutorial set epic is, by scope arithmetic\n74\t  (five curated, release-tested tutorials), above the ~2-week one-sprint epic guideline.\n75\t  Kept as one logical change: all five tutorials are the same work-product type (notebook\n76\t  content), the same team and component, sharing one packaging and validation approach —\n77\t  a split would duplicate the packaging/validation setup and fragment a single content\n78\t  work stream. **Re-split trigger**: re-split this epic if authoring and release-testing\n79\t  the five notebook tutorials exceeds one sprint of effort — split by journey (e.g.\n80\t  first workbench / data prep / first training run vs first deployment / first RAG app).\n81\t\n82\t## Component Mapping Notes\n83\t\n84\t- E001 spans Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines (the format governs all\n85\t  tutorial content); it is assigned the single most-relevant canonical component\n86\t  `Dashboard` because the format is the contract the gallery's launch mechanics parses,\n87\t  and the Dashboard team owns the platform-side contract.\n88\t- E003 is assigned canonical component `Notebooks` (notebook tutorial content running on\n89\t  workbenches) and E004 `Data Science Pipelines` (importable pipeline tutorial) — matching\n90\t  the strategy's Affected Components list and the architecture-context owning teams.\n91\t- `Documentation` has no architecture-context file (expected — it is a docs-content\n92\t  component, not a platform service); the docs epic is routed via the canonical component\n93\t  list, which includes `Documentation`.\n94\t\n95\t## Tiered Delivery\n96\t\n97\tNot applicable: the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain timing (no\n98\tDependencies table, no upstream or vendor coordination), so all work is planned as a\n99\tsingle tier.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dd73da545002e50","agent_id":"ab020e0751ef634b2","session_id":"a13b45e9-5701-490f-bd0b-60390eed1471","uuid":"c5fc7062-84f9-490e-b744-3291f4711f5f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:45:03.793Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f0d0bec8a5d1111","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
