{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e83fabf44f75f99","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Define the tutorial packaging format\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: -1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Define the tutorial packaging format\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers the definition of the tutorial packaging format — the metadata, pinned images,\n34\tand validation manifest that make a tutorial a versioned, independently testable\n35\tpackage. The format is the shared contract between the platform and tutorial content:\n36\tthe tutorial gallery's launch mechanics reads it, and every authored tutorial is\n37\tpackaged in it. Defining it first lets the gallery implementation and the tutorial\n38\tauthoring proceed in parallel against a stable contract.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the tutorial package metadata: identity, description, the journey it covers,\n43\t  and its launch kind (open a workbench with the notebook, or import the pipeline)\n44\t- Define how a tutorial pins the images it runs on, so a tutorial executes against\n45\t  known, fixed images rather than whatever the cluster currently serves\n46\t- Define the validation manifest: the mechanism by which a tutorial's expected behavior\n47\t  is described so the tutorial can be tested against a release\n48\t- Define the versioning scheme for tutorial packages so tutorials are versioned and\n49\t  testable independently of Dashboard releases\n50\t- Publish the format as the agreed contract for the gallery implementation and for\n51\t  tutorial authors\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- The packaging format is documented and covers package metadata, image pinning, and\n56\t  the validation manifest\n57\t- A tutorial package conforming to the format carries a version independent of the\n58\t  Dashboard release cadence\n59\t- A conforming tutorial package can be validated via its manifest against the current\n60\t  release without a Dashboard release\n61\t- The format definition is accepted by the teams that build against it (the gallery\n62\t  implementation and the tutorial authoring teams)\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-3 (P1): a tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation\n67\t  manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of\n68\t  Dashboard releases. The epic is scheduled at P0 by priority inheritance — it gates\n69\t  the tutorial gallery and all tutorial authoring.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9dd73da545002e50","agent_id":"ab020e0751ef634b2","session_id":"a13b45e9-5701-490f-bd0b-60390eed1471","uuid":"b7fb487a-8dae-4ac7-a0f2-13b0410531e8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:45:07.053Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e83fabf44f75f99","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
